# === Rust / Cargo ===
# Ignore build output directories (any crate's target/)
target/
**/target/
Cargo.lock
# Ignore generated documentation and incremental compilation caches
target/doc/
**/target/doc/
target/**/incremental/

# Ignore compiled binary artifacts in common build folders
**/debug/
**/release/

# Keep Cargo.lock for applications (recommended). If you are authoring a library,
# you may choose to ignore Cargo.lock, but it's common to commit it for apps.

# === IDEs / Editors ===
.vscode/
.idea/
*.sublime-project
*.sublime-workspace
*.swp
*.swm
*~

# === macOS / Windows system files ===
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
Desktop.ini

# === Logs, temporary, and misc files ===
*.log
*.tmp
*.temp

# === Rust analyzer / editor caches ===
.rustfmt.toml
/.cargo/
/.rustup/

# === Other common ignores ===
# Node modules (if you ever add a frontend)
node_modules/

# Coverage reports
coverage/

# Secrets and environment files
.env
.env.local

# Ignore compiled artifacts that might be present in subfolders
**/*.exe
**/*.dll
**/*.so
**/*.dylib

# End of .gitignore/target
